v 3
d combineall. Combine (append, merge, or joinby) or convert every file in a directory.
d
d combineall sweeps a directory and combines every file of one type
d (.dta, CSV and other delimited text, Excel, or XML) into a single
d dataset by append, merge, or joinby, or converts the files to .dta
d and stops (convertonly).  The engine dates to 2011 (v1.0.0).
d
d v2.0.0 adds a harmonization layer under cmethod(append) for
d stacking yearly file releases whose element names mutate across
d vintages: map(renames.csv) applies only the renames whose
d [firstyear,lastyear] window covers the 4-digit year extracted
d from each filename, generates int year, records provenance in
d char varname[source], and prints a variable-by-year
d harmonization table.  strict turns absent-oldname reports into
d errors.  Replaces the panelstack package.
d
d   combineall using "built/panel", cmethod(append) map(renames.csv)
d
d Requires: Stata 16+.  No Python or other external dependencies.
d
d KW: append
d KW: merge
d KW: joinby
d KW: import
d KW: convert
d KW: panel
d KW: harmonize
d KW: rename
d KW: vintage
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Sr Researcher, Texas 2036
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d Distribution-Date: 20260706
d
f combineall.ado
f combineall.sthlp
